  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 302 PM EDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nBroad ridging will extend across the southern and southeastern U.S \nas we close out the weekend and head into early next week. As such, \ntemperatures will remain above normal with heat index values over \n100 across the bulk of the area during this time frame. Additional \nHeat Advisories are highly likely to continue for portions of the \narea where heat index values over 105 occur. \n\nBy midweek, the core of the midlevel ridge shifts westward to center \nacross the Southern Plains into the Southwest. As such, the forecast \narea transitions to be on the eastern periphery of the ridge, \nfavoring a return to a pattern more supportive of additional \ndisturbances/thunderstorm complexes working southward, though \ndetails of timing and exact placement of these will be unclear until \nwe get closer to this time frame. Thus, while PoPs remain fairly low \nand of the isolated variety at this juncture, these could certainly \ntrend upward as we get closer to next week.",
